{
  "817": {
    "document_id": "817",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "The release reports that a subcommittee held a hearing on Collins's Social Security Fairness Act and that she testified in support of it. Under negative clarification (6), hearings that seek future action and announce no delivered result are not credit-claiming; the bill remains pending and no outcome (passage, funding, or decision) is claimed as achieved."
  },
  "871": {
    "document_id": "871",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Salazar questions Interior Secretary Norton about proposed budget cuts to PILT, LWCF, and Park Service rules. This is oversight and criticism of the administration under negative clarification (1) (criticism of the administration) and (6) (questioning/letters seeking future action). No benefit is announced as delivered and no result is attributed to Salazar's efforts."
  },
  "1118": {
    "document_id": "1118",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Carper issues a statement explaining his vote against the constitutional amendment banning gay marriage. Under negative clarification (1), vote explanations and position statements are pure position-taking, not credit-claiming. No outcome is attributed to his actions."
  },
  "1177": {
    "document_id": "1177",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Pryor and Chambliss call on the Air Force to reimburse unpaid subcontractors and announce they 'will continue to mount pressure' and pursue a legislative fix. Under negative clarification (6), requests and demands seeking future action that announce no delivered result are not credit-claiming. No reimbursement or other outcome has been achieved."
  },
  "1230": {
    "document_id": "1230",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Harkin and Hatch welcome FDA manufacturing regulations that they, as principal authors of the underlying DSHEA statute, 'have been pushing the FDA to publish for more than a decade.' This matches the codebook's own positive example: credit-claiming for a non-monetary policy outcome achieved through the senators' sustained effort, under clarification (3) (federal decision tied to the senators' advocacy)."
  },
  "1320": {
    "document_id": "1320",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Headlined 'HUTCHISON SECURES DROUGHT, WILDFIRE RELIEF FOR TEXAS,' the release announces passage of an emergency appropriations bill containing $3 billion for disaster relief, with Hutchison stating 'I am pleased to help secure this funding.' This is explicit credit-claiming for federal dollars under clarifications (1) and (2)."
  },
  "1747": {
    "document_id": "1747",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "The release reports that 'The U.S. Senate has approved legislation by Sen. Robert C. Byrd' to boost funding for the National Guard Youth ChalleNGe program, including his provision in the Defense Authorization Bill. Under clarification (4), reporting passage or inclusion of the senator's own provisions is credit-claiming."
  },
  "1862": {
    "document_id": "1862",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Baucus and Tester announce $12.5 million for Butte military projects included in the Defense Appropriations bill, stating they 'delivered on their promise to secure federal funding' and 'were proud to go to bat for these dollars.' This is explicit credit-claiming for federal funds delivered to their state under clarifications (1) and (2), and joint delegation announcements still count."
  },
  "2026": {
    "document_id": "2026",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "The release reports that the Senate Judiciary Committee passed the Leahy-Specter Personal Data Privacy and Security Act, legislation introduced by Chairman Leahy. Under clarification (4), reporting committee approval of the senator's own bill is credit-claiming for a legislative accomplishment."
  },
  "2627": {
    "document_id": "2627",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "This matches the codebook's own positive example: headlined 'TALENT SECURES $1.5 MILLION,' it states the Senate 'approved his request' for the Mizzou research center, and includes officials thanking Talent for securing the money — an explicit claim of personal responsibility for delivered federal funds under clarifications (1) and (2)."
  },
  "2675": {
    "document_id": "2675",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Dodd, Lieberman, and Simmons report meeting with BRAC commissioners to argue against closing Sub Base New London. Under negative clarification (6), meetings that seek future action and announce no delivered result are not credit-claiming; Dodd explicitly notes 'this is only one more step in this marathon' and the base's fate remains pending."
  },
  "3271": {
    "document_id": "3271",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "The release announces unanimous Senate passage of the Financial Services Regulatory Relief Act, 'authored by Idaho Senator Mike Crapo,' and details his leadership of the effort over two years. Under clarification (4), reporting passage of the senator's own bill is credit-claiming for a legislative accomplishment."
  },
  "3477": {
    "document_id": "3477",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Cornyn's office announces as news the Senate confirmation of a Texan to chair the Privacy and Civil Liberties Oversight Board. Under clarification (3), announcing a federal decision benefiting the state — including appointments — counts as credit-claiming when the senator announces it as news; the release also ties Cornyn to the outcome by noting he 'chaired the nominations hearing' for the nominees. I considered coding 0 as mere welcoming without an explicit role claim, but the appointment-announcement-as-news pattern and the reference to his institutional role in the process fit the clarification's credit-claiming criteria."
  },
  "3501": {
    "document_id": "3501",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Tester issues a statement expressing disappointment that the Air Force is targeting missiles at Malmstrom and pledging 'I will continue to fight.' Under negative clarifications (1) and (3), this is position-taking and advocacy on a pending adverse development, claiming no achieved outcome."
  },
  "3534": {
    "document_id": "3534",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Domenici credits President Bush for his gasoline price plan and urges Congress to do more. Under negative clarification (1), this is pure position-taking — praising another actor's proposal — and under (5) it attributes any action to the President, not to Domenici himself. No benefit is announced as delivered and no outcome is attributed to Domenici's efforts."
  },
  "3560": {
    "document_id": "3560",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "The Arkansas delegation announces over $877,000 in HUD grants awarded to housing agencies across Arkansas, with a detailed list of recipients. Under clarification (1), announcing federal grants coming to the senator's state is credit-claiming even without an explicit 'I secured,' because the announcement associates the delegation with the benefit; joint delegation announcements still count."
  },
  "3729": {
    "document_id": "3729",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Grassley announces that President Bush has named Matt Dummermuth interim U.S. Attorney for the Northern District of Iowa, and notes Dummermuth 'was one of three names Grassley nominated to fill the opening.' Under clarification (3), this announces a federal appointment benefiting the state and explicitly ties it to the senator's own recommendation, making it credit-claiming."
  },
  "3744": {
    "document_id": "3744",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Inouye announces as news that the CDC plans to establish a field station in Hawaii for Asia-Pacific disease detection, a federal decision benefiting his state under clarification (3). The release also explicitly claims a previously delivered benefit — noting the CDC earlier established an occupational health center in Hilo 'at Senator Inouye's request' — which independently qualifies under clarification (6)."
  },
  "3845": {
    "document_id": "3845",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Bayh responds to OPEC's decision by touting his pending energy bill and urging Congress to 'pass my plan' when it returns. Under negative clarifications (1) and (2), this is position-taking and advocacy for pending legislation; no outcome is claimed as achieved."
  },
  "4531": {
    "document_id": "4531",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Thune and Clinton announce they have introduced legislation to extend child care benefits for families of fallen soldiers. Under negative clarification (2), introducing a bill is position-taking, not an accomplishment; no passage or delivered benefit is claimed. References to other past cosponsorships are incidental background to the announcement of the new bill."
  }
}
